# Supply-chain cooldown.
#
# npm resolves a dependency tree only from versions published more than this many
# days ago. npm 11.10+ supports it but leaves it off; pnpm 11 defaults to one day
# and Yarn 4.10 to three, so three days is the conservative end of current
# practice without stalling legitimate updates for long.
#
# It exists because the npm attacks that matter now are zero-day publishes from a
# hijacked maintainer account, not old known-bad versions. Shai-Hulud V2 moved
# from the postinstall hook to preinstall in November 2025, so even a failed
# install executes the payload, and the Mini Shai-Hulud waves ran from
# 2026-04-29 into May 2026. Those campaigns are detected and yanked within hours
# to a day or two; a cooldown is what keeps this repo from installing inside that
# window.
#
# Note this does NOT affect `npm ci`, which installs exactly what the lockfile
# already pins. It applies when the tree is (re)built: `npm install`, `npm update`,
# adding a dependency. To take a fresh release deliberately, pass
# `--min-release-age=0` for that one command rather than editing this file.
min-release-age=3
